        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1000]\nBoth, the r- and the s-values shall always be transferred with their maximum length. If any of these values is shorter, it shall be filled up with leading zeros. The receiver shall assign the first half of the bytes to r and the second half of the bytes to s. This encoding is described in IETF RFC 4050:2005, 3.3.",
